---
description: Bump a gem version once per branch and ship upgrade notes instead of shims
alwaysApply: true
---

On a gem repo, if you are not on the default branch, bump the gem version once for the whole branch.

Fetch the remote default branch before you pick the number. Your version must be strictly greater than default. Never reuse a version that already shipped, and never go backwards.

Do not bump again on the same branch unless that version already merged or default caught up. Recheck after you rebase or merge default, and again right before you commit.

Write release notes for what changed. If implementation, config, public API, dependencies, or behavior changed, add short upgrade notes. Prefer clean code over compatibility shims: ship the notes, the upgrade code, and tests that the upgrade worked.

A GitHub Release on the version tag is how a bump ships. Do not tag from a still-open version PR.
